WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.322
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.322 --> 00:00:04.850
- [Narrator] This is Julia,
a Thick Billed Parrot.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:07.365
They are the only surviving parrot species

00:00:07.365 --> 00:00:09.365
native to North America.

00:00:13.695 --> 00:00:16.553
A combination of the illegal
pet trade, habitat loss,

00:00:16.553 --> 00:00:19.280
and global warming has
left this beautiful bird

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.358
endangered in the wild.

00:00:21.358 --> 00:00:23.845
These medium sized
parrots are bright green

00:00:23.845 --> 00:00:25.754
with a black beak and red markings

00:00:25.754 --> 00:00:28.719
on their head, shoulders, and legs.

00:00:28.719 --> 00:00:31.891
The majority of their diet
is composed of pine seeds,

00:00:31.891 --> 00:00:36.037
but they also feed on berries,
insects and tree bark.

00:00:36.037 --> 00:00:38.153
Their thick bill is
capable of breaking through

00:00:38.153 --> 00:00:40.839
practically every nut on earth.

00:00:40.839 --> 00:00:43.768
Thick Billed Parrots live in
high elevation pine forests

00:00:43.768 --> 00:00:45.683
in northern Mexico.

00:00:45.683 --> 00:00:48.649
They used to be found in
Arizona and New Mexico,

00:00:48.649 --> 00:00:50.640
but because of hunting and predation,

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.635
they haven't been seen
in the United States

00:00:52.635 --> 00:00:54.954
for over 20 years.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:56.785
Experts estimate that there are only

00:00:56.785 --> 00:00:59.452
three to 6,000 left in the wild.

